00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:42.000
And that's something the yodel certainly evokes. The other thing that this song speaks to is an undercurrent throughout the history of country music, which is the erasure of the way black artists contributed to the origins of the genre. The seven musical magpies, Clarence Williams, Sarah Martin, Eva Taylor. these were all black artists and they're playing with the same influences as Jimmy Rogers. They're doing it earlier than him. But as the record industry built up, they were not the ones ultimately to profit from it. Yeah, it's another story that we hear over and over again across all of recorded music.
这也是约德尔唱法肯定会唤起的东西。这首歌所谈论的另一件事是贯穿乡村音乐历史的一股暗流，即黑人艺术家对该流派起源的贡献被抹杀了。“七只音乐喜鹊”、克拉伦斯·威廉姆斯、莎拉·马丁、伊娃·泰勒，这些都是黑人艺术家，他们演奏着与吉米·罗杰斯相同的影响。他们比他更早这样做。但随着唱片业的建立，他们最终并不是从中获利的人。是的，这是我们在所有录制音乐中一遍又一遍听到的另一个故事。

